<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arduin Glaber</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 977</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arduin Glaber was a 10th-century count who received control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a> and the Susa valley around 941 and founded the March of Turin. He drove the Saracens of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fraxinetum">Fraxinetum</a> from the Alpine passes. His great-granddaughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adelaide-of-susa">Adelaide of Susa</a> brought his lands to the house of Savoy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arduin-glaber.jpg" alt="Arduin Glaber" width="320" height="291" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marchese Arduino · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ardouin_(comte_de_Turin).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
